        "detailed_description": "<ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Casual isometric point and click murder mystery game</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Procedurally generated mansion, suspects, weapons, and motives</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Locked rooms deepen the mystery, find the keys and unlock the secrets</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Two visual play styles: full color or black &amp; white noir ambiance</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 real time hour to solve the crime. No saves.</strong><br><strong></strong><br><strong> Step Into the Role of a Classic Detective:</strong></p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Interview Intriguing Guests</strong> – Question unique suspects and uncover hidden motives through dynamic conversations. All suspects are procedurally generated so names, professions, motives, relationships are unique every time.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hunt for the Murder Weapon</strong> – Search a manor filled with everyday objects... but only one is the killer’s tool. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Match</strong> <strong>Fingerprints</strong> - Collect fingerprints from objects or ask the suspects. Some will comply, some don't.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Solve the Case</strong> – Get the weapon, identify the culprit, and make the arrest. You have one hour before the police arrives and takes over the investigation, ruining your detective reputation.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Explore a New Manor Every Time</strong> – Investigate a procedurally-generated 3-story mansion with secrets behind every door.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Choose Your Vibe</strong> – Immerse yourself in rich color or switch to noir black &amp; white for that classic detective feel.</p></li></ul>",
        "about_the_game": "<ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Casual isometric point and click murder mystery game</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Procedurally generated mansion, suspects, weapons, and motives</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Locked rooms deepen the mystery, find the keys and unlock the secrets</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Two visual play styles: full color or black &amp; white noir ambiance</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1 real time hour to solve the crime. No saves.</strong><br><strong></strong><br><strong> Step Into the Role of a Classic Detective:</strong></p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Interview Intriguing Guests</strong> – Question unique suspects and uncover hidden motives through dynamic conversations. All suspects are procedurally generated so names, professions, motives, relationships are unique every time.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Hunt for the Murder Weapon</strong> – Search a manor filled with everyday objects... but only one is the killer’s tool. </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Match</strong> <strong>Fingerprints</strong> - Collect fingerprints from objects or ask the suspects. Some will comply, some don't.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Solve the Case</strong> – Get the weapon, identify the culprit, and make the arrest. You have one hour before the police arrives and takes over the investigation, ruining your detective reputation.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Explore a New Manor Every Time</strong> – Investigate a procedurally-generated 3-story mansion with secrets behind every door.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Choose Your Vibe</strong> – Immerse yourself in rich color or switch to noir black &amp; white for that classic detective feel.</p></li></ul>",
        "short_description": "Death in the Manor is a casual isometric point and click murder mystery game. You have 1 hour to discover the killer and weapon before the police arrives. Every game is procedurally generated: rooms change place, suspects are never the same, and there are 22 potential murder weapons.",
